  "description": "issue #766: the addressed turtle set is observable in the trace stream, so a consumer can satisfy spec/rendering.md:191 (\"Implementations with multiple turtles MUST identify the active turtle or addressed turtle set\"). This is that issue's first acceptance criterion verbatim: `tell [ :a :b ]` / `forward 10` / `ask :b [ hide_turtle ]`. Each change of the addressed set emits a `primitive` event — the registered generic catch-all for a primitive without a more specific kind (spec/execution-model.md:703), NOT a new event kind — carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }`. The snapshot is absolute, so folding the stream by assignment yields the addressed set { 1, 2 } and current turtle 1 after `ask` restores (spec/turtles-and-sprites.md:58), even though the last turtle-stamped effect in the stream belongs to turtle 2. An addressing event describes a SET, so it carries no envelope `turtle_id` (spec/execution-model.md:638: present only when the event is turtle-specific).",
